{"key":"enterprise/T1556.008","id":"T1556.008","name":"Network Provider DLL","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1556","tactics":["credential-access","defense-impairment","persistence"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may register malicious network provider dynamic link libraries (DLLs) to capture cleartext user credentials during the authentication process. Network provider DLLs allow Windows to interface with specific network protocols and can also support add-on credential management functions. During the logon process, Winlogon (the interactive logon module) sends credentials to the local `mpnotify.exe` process via RPC. The `mpnotify.exe`…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1556/008","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--90c4a591-d02d-490b-92aa-619d9701ac04","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.705Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0580","name":"Detect Network Provider DLL Registration and Credential Capture","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstr